<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaffna Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 13th century–1619</span> · Also known as Kingdom of Jaffna, Aryacakravarti dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jaffna Kingdom was a Tamil kingdom in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> ruled by the Aryacakravarti dynasty, whose origins are connected with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> expeditions to the island in the late 13th century. Centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffna">Jaffna</a> peninsula, it controlled the pearl fisheries at times and rivalled the Sinhalese kingdoms, until the Portuguese conquered it in 1619.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaffna-kingdom.jpg" alt="Jaffna Kingdom" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AntanO via Taprobanus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jaffna_Kingdom.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
